--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: ToRiverwood
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I never really gave much appreciation to my walks to school.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474705638883538
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I imagine this would suck way more if I didn't walk regularly.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Then again, the hills do make this definetively worse than the walk to
      school.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Also the lack of Sayori. That doesn't help either.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: After a few minutes of walking, I come upon the Guardian Stones.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474728083652608
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: In the game, interacting with them would give you a permanent buff.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: For these three, it would be an increase to experience gained for the
      skills that correspond to Warriors, Mages, and Thieves.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... I wonder what they'd do for me?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I walk up next to the Warrior Stone, the one I usually go with.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Standing next to it, I can feel something...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I would say magical, but I feel like that wouldn't be accurate.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I reach out my hand to touch the stone...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: At my touch, the stone lights up, projecting a beacon into the sky.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I feel... something?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: What it did to me, I'm not sure, but I guess it'd be better to have its
      boon than to not.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: With archaic rock power flowing through me(?), I continue my journey
      to Riverwood.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: After another few minutes, and a couple encounters with unfriendly fauna,
      I arrive to Riverwood.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474728083652660
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Remember not to hit the chicken!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Alright, time to take stock of my situation.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Foreign land, no money, I have a weapon, but no food.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 'Hmm. '
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I suppose there's nothing stopping me from getting help from both Alvor
      and Gerdur...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: If I remember right, Gerdur should have food, Alvor has smithing materials,
      and both should have some gold they can spare me...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions: []
